σὺν γλυκεῖ δὲ καὶ κονίᾳ τοῖς κώνειον ἢ μηκώνιον, σὺν ὀξυμέλιτι δὲ τοῖς γύψον ἢ ἐφήμερον πεπωκόσι, πρὸς δὲ τὰ σπάσματα καὶ ῥήγματα καὶ ὕδρωπας μετὰ συκίου βιβρωσκομένη. ξηρὰ δὲ ποθεῖσα ὀξυβάφου πλῆθος σὺν μελικράτῳ μέλανα κατὰ κοιλίαν ἄγει, ἔμμηνά τε κινεῖ καὶ βῆχας θεραπεύει σὺν μέλιτι ἐκλειχομένη· καὶ κνησμοὺς δὲ καὶ ψώραν καὶ ἴκτερον τὸ ἀφέψημα αὐτῆς ἐν λουτρῷ ὠφελεῖ. ὁ δὲ χυλὸς αὐτῆς χλωρᾶς οὔσης παρίσθμια καὶ κιονίδας καὶ ἄφθας θεραπεύει καὶ αἷμα διὰ ῥινῶν ἄγει σὺν ἐλαίῳ ἰρίνῳ ἐγχυματιζόμενος· σὺν γάλακτι δὲ καὶ ὠταλγίας παρηγορεῖ ἐμετικόν τε φάρμακον δι᾿ αὐτῆς σκευάζεται καὶ κρομύων καὶ ῥοὸς τοῦ ἐπὶ τὰ ὄψα, πάντων ἐν χαλκῷ Κυπρίῳ ἐν τοῖς ὑπὸ κύνα καύμασιν ἡλιασθέντων ἐπὶ ἡμέρας τεσσαράκοντα· ὑποστρωννυμένη δὲ ἡ πόα ἐρπετὰ διώκει.","spans":[{"start":232,"end":241,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":334,"end":339,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":355,"end":362,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":368,"end":372,"concept_id":"bruises","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":380,"end":385,"concept_id":"edema_dropsy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":467,"end":479,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":486,"end":501,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":506,"end":509,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":550,"end":555,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":566,"end":571,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":576,"end":581,"concept_id":"jaundice","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":649,"end":656,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":663,"end":669,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":676,"end":681,"concept_id":"mouth_gums","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":696,"end":710,"concept_id":"nosebleed","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":768,"end":773,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":787,"end":793,"concept_id":"nausea_vomiting","polarity":"action"},{"start":976,"end":987,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"action"}]},"dsc:3.29":{"ref":"De materia medica 3.29","headword":"ἡ δὲ ἀγριορίγανος","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"ἡ δὲ ἀγριορίγανος, ἣν πάνακες ἢ Ἡρακλείαν ἢ κονίλην καλοῦσιν, ὧν ἐστι καὶ Νίκανδρος ὁ Κολοφώνιος (Th. sq.)· ἔχει τὰ μὲν φύλλα ὀριγάνῳ ὅμοια, ῥαβδία δὲ σπιθαμιαῖα, λεπτά, ἐφ᾿ ὧν σκιάδια ὅμοια ἀνήθῳ· ἄνθη δὲ λευκά, ῥίζα λεπτή, ἄχρηστος. ἰδίως δὲ βοηθεῖ θηριοδήκτοις τὰ φύλλα καὶ τὰ ἄνθη σὺν οἴνῳ πινόμενα.","spans":[{"start":251,"end":260,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"}]},"dsc:5.51":{"ref":"De materia medica 5.51","headword":"οἶνος ὀριγανίτης διʼ","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"οἶνος ὀριγανίτης διʼ ὀριγάνου Ἡρακλεωτικῆς σκευάζεται ὁμοίως τῷ θυμίτῃ, ποιῶν πρὸς τὰ αὐτά.","spans":[]},"cul:192-wind-marjoram":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Wind Marjoram","headword":"Wind Marjoram","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"This is also under the dominion of Mercury. It strengthens the stomach and head much, there being scarce a better remedy growing for such as are troubled with a sour humour in the stomach; it restores the appetite being lost; helps the cough, and consumption of the lungs; it cleanses the body of choler, expels poison, and remedies the infirmities of the spleen; helps the bitings of venomous beasts, and helps such as have poisoned themselves by eating Hemlock, Henbane, or Opium. It provokes urine and the terms in women, helps the dropsy, and the scurvy, scabs, itch, and yellow jaundice. The juice being dropped into the ears, helps deafness, pain and noise in the ears. And thus much for this herb, between which and adders, there is a deadly antipathy.","spans":[{"start":47,"end":70,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":161,"end":187,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":205,"end":213,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":236,"end":241,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":247,"end":258,"concept_id":"tuberculosis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":312,"end":318,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":356,"end":362,"concept_id":"spleen_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":374,"end":384,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":385,"end":393,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":486,"end":514,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":535,"end":541,"concept_id":"edema_dropsy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":551,"end":557,"concept_id":"scurvy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":559,"end":564,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":566,"end":570,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":583,"end":591,"concept_id":"jaundice","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":617,"end":646,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":648,"end":674,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":723,"end":729,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"dsc:3.27":{"232":"bitten by wild beasts (θηριόδηκτοι)","334":"those who have drunk (a poison) (πεπωκότες)","355":"spasms, strains (σπάσματα)","368":"ruptures, strains (ῥήγματα)","380":"dropsy (ὕδρωψ, ὑδρωπικοί)","467":"purges downwards (κατὰ κοιλίαν)","486":"brings on the menses (emmenagogue)","506":"cough (βήξ, βήσσοντες)","550":"itching (κνησμός)","566":"itch, scabies (ψώρα)","576":"jaundice (ἴκτερος, ἰκτερικοί)","649":"tonsils / tonsillitis (παρίσθμια)","663":"(relaxed) uvula (κιονίς)","676":"aphthae (mouth ulcers)","696":"bleeding from the nostrils","768":"earache (ὠταλγία)","787":"emetic (ἐμετικός, ἐμετήριον)","976":"drives away snakes / beasts (repellent)"},"dsc:3.29":{"251":"bitten by wild beasts (θηριόδηκτοι)"},"cul:192-wind-marjoram":{"47":"strengthens / comforts the stomach (stomachic)","161":"pains / gnawing / heat of the stomach","205":"appetite (provokes / restores)","236":"cough, coughs","247":"consumption (phthisis), esp. of the lungs","312":"resists / expels poison","356":"spleen: hardness, swelling, stoppings of the spleen","374":"biting / stinging of (serpents, scorpions, beasts)","385":"venomous beasts / creatures","486":"provokes / brings down the terms, courses: emmenagogue","535":"dropsy, dropsies","551":"scurvy","559":"scabs: scabies / scabby skin","566":"itch, itches, itching","583":"yellow jaundice, black jaundice","617":"dropped into the ears, eases the pains / kills the worms","648":"pains / noise / singing / worms in the ears","723":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps"}},"images":[]}